A poor young girl is sent out into the freezing streets on New Year¡¯s Eve to sell matches. She is barefoot, cold, and afraid to return home because she hasn¡¯t sold anything and her father will be angry. To keep warm, she lights matches one by one.
Each match creates a brief vision: a warm stove, a festive Christmas dinner, a beautiful Christmas tree, and finally her kind grandmother, the only person who ever loved her. When she lights the last matches, she sees her grandmother¡¯s spirit and asks to go with her. The next morning, people find the girl frozen to death, but she is smiling peacefully, as if she has found warmth and happiness in heaven.
The story is basically about extreme poverty, loneliness, and how imagination becomes an escape from suffering.
